143:**Landing paired lobu + owletto PRs:** merge the owletto PR (squash), take the resulting owletto-main SHA, re-point the lobu submodule pointer PR at *that squash SHA*, then merge lobu. `check-drift` fails until the pointer is an ancestor of owletto/main. When the pointer branch is behind lobu main, use `git merge origin/main` — **never `git rebase`**, which drops the pointer commit as "patch contents already upstream", after which a `--amend` corrupts HEAD. To recover, first make the damage reversible — `git status` must be clean (stop if it is not, and commit rather than discard), then tag the current tip so nothing is stranded: `git branch backup/<branch>-$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)`. Only then reset to the remote tip with `git reset --keep origin/<branch>` (it refuses rather than clobbering uncommitted work; use `--hard` only on a confirmed-clean tree). Then merge and resolve the single submodule conflict:
