../../packages/owletto/DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md:35:- **Index/landing pages are header + one body region.** A section's index route (`/$owner/connectors`, `/$owner/agents`) renders the page header, then exactly one body region: a `<TabEmptyState>` onboarding CTA when the collection is empty (*"Create your first connection"*), or the collection when it isn't. Agents use a responsive card grid (`grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`); Connectors use the bordered row list in §12. Don't inline create-forms or catalogs on the index page — those are their own routes (`/connectors/create`, `/agents/create`), reached from the sidebar or the empty-state CTA's action. **Don't put a stats/sparkline strip on a management index.** A list of configured things (agents, connectors) is a management surface, not a dashboard — "how many agents over 14 days" is vanity chrome there, so those pages lead with the body region. Add a volume strip only where the count over time *is* the point of the page. **Entity cards reuse the picker-card recipe** (clickable filled card, no border, `text-muted-foreground` → `hover:text-foreground`, `hover:bg-accent/50`): a status dot / `ConnectorMark` + name on the first row and an optional 2-line `line-clamp-2` description. A muted metadata row pinned to the bottom with `mt-auto` is **optional** — include it only for genuinely functional metadata (a connection's feed count), never engagement-vanity counts (users / behaviors / apps on an agent card). The whole card is a router `<Link>` to the item's detail route — so one consistent box style covers catalog pickers, index lists, and the sidebar.
